---
import ResourceArticle from "@/layouts/ResourceArticle.astro";
import { resources } from "@/lib/resources";
---
<ResourceArticle page={resources.expressions}>
  <p>Enter a full expression in Eva|Bar’s menu bar calculator to see the answer update as you type. Use a period for decimals and commas between function arguments.</p>

  <h2>Expressions to try</h2>
  <table class="resource-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Expression</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Apply a 15% discount to 240</th><td><code>240 * (1 - 15 / 100)</code></td><td>204</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Average three values</th><td><code>avg(12,18,24)</code></td><td>18</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Find a remainder</th><td><code>17 % 5</code></td><td>2</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Combine a power and a square root</th><td><code>2^3 + sqrt(81)</code></td><td>17</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Use a base-3 logarithm</th><td><code>log(81,3)</code></td><td>4</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Find the sine of 30 degrees</th><td><code>sin(30 * pi / 180)</code></td><td>0.5</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The discount example divides by 100 to turn 15% into a decimal. To calculate the discount amount itself, enter <code>240 * 15 / 100</code> to get <strong>36</strong>. Use the <code>%</code> operator when you want the remainder of a division, as in <code>17 % 5</code>.</p>
  <p>In the sine example, <code>30 * pi / 180</code> converts 30 degrees to radians. Use the same conversion whenever you pass an angle in degrees to <code>sin()</code>, <code>cos()</code>, or <code>tan()</code>.</p>

  <h2>Find functions in the app</h2>
  <p>If you need a function beyond the examples above, open the <strong>f</strong> panel for the built-in reference. Alongside <code>avg()</code>, you’ll find <code>min()</code> and <code>max()</code> for the smallest and largest values in a list. Use <code>round()</code> for the nearest integer, or <code>floor()</code> and <code>ceil()</code> to round down and up, respectively.</p>

  <h2>Control the format of copied results</h2>
  <p>Once you have your answer, press <kbd>Return</kbd> to copy it. If you need a specific format for a spreadsheet or report, open <strong>… → Preferences</strong> and set the number of decimal places and the decimal and thousands separators. The format applies to both displayed and copied results. Keep using a period when you enter a decimal in an expression, even if the result displays a comma.</p>
</ResourceArticle>
